381
00:22:53,607 --> 00:22:55,676
In the Cheer Performance Mission,

382
00:22:55,677 --> 00:22:58,006
the sport I'm cheering for is swimming.

383
00:22:58,007 --> 00:23:01,546
Since I was little, I was very familiar with swimming.

384
00:23:01,547 --> 00:23:04,416
It's because my older cousin...

385
00:23:04,417 --> 00:23:06,446
was a former national swim team member.

386
00:23:06,447 --> 00:23:07,963
(A former national swim team member, Jeong Doo Hee)

387
00:23:07,987 --> 00:23:10,116
Hello. I'm a former national swim team member,

388
00:23:10,117 --> 00:23:11,557
Jeong Doo Hee.

389
00:23:11,857 --> 00:23:14,386
Having a family member who's a national team member...

390
00:23:14,387 --> 00:23:15,796
is something not common.

391
00:23:15,797 --> 00:23:17,796
He spent time as an athlete...

392
00:23:17,797 --> 00:23:20,567
and I could listen to his story by his side.

393
00:23:20,667 --> 00:23:22,336
I was inspired by his stories,

394
00:23:22,337 --> 00:23:25,136
and decided to incorporate the inspiration into my performance.

395
00:23:25,137 --> 00:23:27,007
That's why I chose swimming.

396
00:23:27,107 --> 00:23:29,406
He said swimming is a sport...

397
00:23:29,407 --> 00:23:31,106
which is a battle against oneself.

398
00:23:31,107 --> 00:23:32,806
Without brutally honest self-assessment,

399
00:23:32,807 --> 00:23:35,977
breaking records is simply out of the question.

400
00:23:36,077 --> 00:23:38,786
You need to keep breaking your own records...

401
00:23:38,787 --> 00:23:40,286
and someone else's records.

402
00:23:40,287 --> 00:23:42,757
It's a battle against your limits, according to my cousin.

403
00:23:42,857 --> 00:23:44,956
I think I'm in a similar situation.

404
00:23:44,957 --> 00:23:47,726
Being in this survival show,

405
00:23:47,727 --> 00:23:49,697
I've competed with many people,

406
00:23:49,797 --> 00:23:53,397
but I think the biggest battle has been against myself.

407
00:23:53,497 --> 00:23:55,467
Meanwhile, I've experienced frustration,

408
00:23:55,697 --> 00:23:57,036
hardships,

409
00:23:57,037 --> 00:23:58,736
and I've often faced my limits.

410
00:23:58,737 --> 00:24:01,836
But in the end, I've come to the final.

411
00:24:01,837 --> 00:24:05,276
Therefore, for swimmers battling against themselves,

412
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:07,976
I'd like to give a message that they can move forward.

413
00:24:07,977 --> 00:24:11,216
I want the music to be grand but have a calm, serene feel.

414
00:24:11,217 --> 00:24:14,316
There's a point I definitely want to convey.

415
00:24:14,317 --> 00:24:18,056
Beneath the water and above the water as two different realms...

416
00:24:18,057 --> 00:24:20,987
The concept of the performance I prepared...

417
00:24:21,087 --> 00:24:24,526
is built on a clash of the self, where above the water...

418
00:24:24,527 --> 00:24:28,096
represents the exterior, while beneath it represents the interior.

419
00:24:28,097 --> 00:24:31,567
You can be free above the water, and there are many kinds of sounds.

420
00:24:33,937 --> 00:24:36,806
However, beneath the water, you feel much resistance...

421
00:24:36,807 --> 00:24:38,136
and you are alone there.

422
00:24:38,137 --> 00:24:41,006
In that respect, I think the battle against oneself...

423
00:24:41,007 --> 00:24:43,216
happens beneath the water.

424
00:24:43,217 --> 00:24:45,716
Depending on whether the soundproof door is closed or open,

425
00:24:45,717 --> 00:24:46,916
- the sound changes, you know. - Right.

426
00:24:46,917 --> 00:24:49,456
I want to express it with a musical effect.

427
00:24:49,457 --> 00:24:51,086
I want to show a sudden twist.

428
00:24:51,087 --> 00:24:53,456
The sound goes from loud...

429
00:24:53,457 --> 00:24:55,427
to muffled, like this.

430
00:24:55,657 --> 00:24:58,827
So I thought hard about how to represent the texture of the music.

431
00:24:58,927 --> 00:25:01,427
Let's set up the fabric.

432
00:25:01,527 --> 00:25:04,136
Using fabric, I divided above and below the water surface...

433
00:25:04,137 --> 00:25:07,206
to make a wow point of the performance.

434
00:25:07,207 --> 00:25:09,877
Above the water, I wanted to express my exterior,

435
00:25:09,977 --> 00:25:12,646
and below the water, my interior...

436
00:25:12,647 --> 00:25:14,976
battling against myself and repressed.

437
00:25:14,977 --> 00:25:17,546
And contemporary dancers will join the performance.

438
00:25:17,547 --> 00:25:19,186
The dancers are here!

439
00:25:19,187 --> 00:25:21,017
(Son Gwang Bin, Park Jin Ho, Kim Tae Hyeon)

440
00:25:22,257 --> 00:25:23,956
They're precious beings who will pull me up...

441
00:25:23,957 --> 00:25:25,826
