567
00:34:14,317 --> 00:34:15,486
Well,

568
00:34:15,487 --> 00:34:18,957
I always say as a dancer, as a choreographer,

569
00:34:19,727 --> 00:34:22,756
that when you have a theme or a message,

570
00:34:22,757 --> 00:34:25,896
or something that you're trying to get across to your audience,

571
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:27,626
it can be a really big challenge.

572
00:34:27,627 --> 00:34:28,766
It can be ambitious.

573
00:34:28,767 --> 00:34:31,066
It can be a big ask of the audience...

574
00:34:31,067 --> 00:34:32,667
to understand your concepts.

575
00:34:32,807 --> 00:34:34,367
And I feel like,

576
00:34:34,467 --> 00:34:36,806
whether it was inside of the choreography,

577
00:34:36,807 --> 00:34:38,676
whether you were using the prop,

578
00:34:38,677 --> 00:34:40,276
or in the staging,

579
00:34:40,277 --> 00:34:42,946
you always had fluidity...

580
00:34:42,947 --> 00:34:46,086
in the motion of waves going on.

581
00:34:46,087 --> 00:34:47,386
And...

582
00:34:47,387 --> 00:34:50,386
when you have something like that, and you continue to bring it back,

583
00:34:50,387 --> 00:34:51,686
I think that people...

584
00:34:51,687 --> 00:34:53,486
Even if they don't understand every detail,

585
00:34:53,487 --> 00:34:56,396
they subconsciously understand everything.

586
00:34:56,397 --> 00:34:59,196
And for me, the part that stood out the most...

587
00:34:59,197 --> 00:35:01,926
was going up and above the water.

588
00:35:01,927 --> 00:35:03,796
Below and above the water.

589
00:35:03,797 --> 00:35:05,036
Because...

590
00:35:05,037 --> 00:35:07,136
it's something that we've all felt before,

591
00:35:07,137 --> 00:35:10,776
but it would be hard to translate on the ground.

592
00:35:10,777 --> 00:35:13,346
And I really understood the concept.

593
00:35:13,347 --> 00:35:15,376
That would be challenging...

594
00:35:15,377 --> 00:35:18,446
with the sheets and within choreography.

595
00:35:18,447 --> 00:35:19,616
And I thought you did a great job.

596
00:35:19,617 --> 00:35:21,146
So, I think you should be really proud of yourself.

597
00:35:21,147 --> 00:35:23,016
I think your message got across really well.

598
00:35:23,017 --> 00:35:24,117
Good job.

599
00:35:26,527 --> 00:35:27,856
Thank you for your comment,

600
00:35:27,857 --> 00:35:30,257
Ian Eastwood, our special judge.

601
00:35:30,527 --> 00:35:33,826
Director BADA has finished...

602
00:35:33,827 --> 00:35:36,266
her entire performance...

603
00:35:36,267 --> 00:35:38,497
from the teaser to today's live performance.

604
00:35:38,837 --> 00:35:41,036
