641
00:38:43,387 --> 00:38:45,416
For the Cheer Performance Mission,

642
00:38:45,417 --> 00:38:49,397
Koo Young has chosen the marathon.

643
00:38:49,897 --> 00:38:52,766
A sport where everyone runs at their own pace,

644
00:38:52,767 --> 00:38:55,607
yet moves forward to the finish line supported by each other, marathon.

645
00:38:55,997 --> 00:38:59,337
How did he capture the true power of unwavering commitment...

646
00:38:59,467 --> 00:39:02,877
and support through his performance?

647
00:39:03,837 --> 00:39:05,476
Director Back Koo Young's...

648
00:39:05,477 --> 00:39:07,246
Cheer Performance Mission...

649
00:39:07,247 --> 00:39:09,347
begins now!

650
00:39:11,047 --> 00:39:13,247
Ready, fight.

651
00:39:17,157 --> 00:39:19,787
(On the set of the teaser shoot)

652
00:39:20,987 --> 00:39:23,597
The sport that I'll be rooting for is...

653
00:39:23,797 --> 00:39:24,997
marathon.

654
00:39:25,127 --> 00:39:26,766
I believe...

655
00:39:26,767 --> 00:39:29,697
a marathon has a lot in common with a person's life.

656
00:39:30,197 --> 00:39:32,737
They say, "Life is a marathon."

657
00:39:33,007 --> 00:39:34,966
When I look at marathon runners,

658
00:39:34,967 --> 00:39:37,337
they give me this feeling of comfort.

659
00:39:39,307 --> 00:39:40,876
- Please excuse me. - Come on in.

660
00:39:40,877 --> 00:39:43,116
I've been going around because of our outfits.

661
00:39:43,117 --> 00:39:46,617
(He visited the directors' rooms to check his outfit.)

662
00:39:46,747 --> 00:39:48,863
I told you that I took a tour around their rooms, right?

663
00:39:48,887 --> 00:39:50,957
Tae Woo also had a trophy in his room.

664
00:39:50,987 --> 00:39:51,987
It was the Choreographer of the Year...

665
00:39:51,988 --> 00:39:53,686
from Billboard or something.

666
00:39:53,687 --> 00:39:55,997
It was in 2024 or something.

667
00:39:56,097 --> 00:39:59,227
All the other directors have that.

668
00:39:59,327 --> 00:40:00,526
It's the championship trophy.

669
00:40:00,527 --> 00:40:02,243
I won this trophy on "Street Dance Girls Fighter."

670
00:40:02,267 --> 00:40:04,237
My precious awards.

671
00:40:04,397 --> 00:40:05,566
I won first place.

672
00:40:05,567 --> 00:40:07,436
I'm the only Korean to own this.

673
00:40:07,437 --> 00:40:08,507
My trophies.

674
00:40:10,077 --> 00:40:11,107
But...

675
00:40:12,477 --> 00:40:13,577
I don't.

676
00:40:14,777 --> 00:40:16,846
(His cabinet has a family photo...)

677
00:40:16,847 --> 00:40:18,747
(instead of trophies.)

678
00:40:18,847 --> 00:40:21,916
Although I've been dancing...

679
00:40:21,917 --> 00:40:24,517
longer than they have,

680
00:40:24,687 --> 00:40:28,227
I have no experience in achieving such things.

681
00:40:28,987 --> 00:40:30,697
We didn't have the grand award...

682
00:40:30,857 --> 00:40:33,027
for choreographers in my days.

683
00:40:33,297 --> 00:40:35,267
That's when I realized that,

684
00:40:35,397 --> 00:40:38,366
although I'm the oldest and have the most experience...

685
00:40:38,367 --> 00:40:39,767
among all the participants,

686
00:40:41,237 --> 00:40:44,107
perhaps I've accomplished the least.

687
00:40:45,837 --> 00:40:47,506
But in marathons,

688
00:40:47,507 --> 00:40:51,677
you don't see anything fancy or achievements along the way.

689
00:40:51,847 --> 00:40:53,617
It's rather a sport...

690
00:40:53,717 --> 00:40:56,787
in which you quietly run toward the finish line at your own pace.

691
00:40:57,187 --> 00:41:00,957
Marathon and I are very similar.

692
00:41:01,557 --> 00:41:04,297
To give back the comfort I felt...

693
00:41:04,527 --> 00:41:06,967
from marathon to the people...

694
00:41:07,067 --> 00:41:09,397
in my own language on the stage,

695
00:41:09,637 --> 00:41:11,837
I chose this sport.

696
00:41:12,237 --> 00:41:13,906
The key message is,

697
00:41:13,907 --> 00:41:16,177
"Run alone, but never alone."

698
00:41:16,377 --> 00:41:18,136
There was one video...

699
00:41:18,137 --> 00:41:20,907
of the Boston Marathon that gave me strength.

700
00:41:21,077 --> 00:41:23,047
A runner's legs gave out, and he fell.

701
00:41:23,317 --> 00:41:25,947
And another runner came...

702
00:41:26,187 --> 00:41:27,416
to help him up...

703
00:41:27,417 --> 00:41:29,817
and keep running.

704
00:41:30,157 --> 00:41:31,957
Everyone else is running on their own.

705
00:41:32,257 --> 00:41:35,027
But they're not running by themselves.

706
00:41:35,257 --> 00:41:36,496
They're running together, in fact.

707
00:41:36,497 --> 00:41:39,997
I wanted to pay homage to that moment through this.

708
00:41:40,367 --> 00:41:42,736
There's something I'd like to add.

709
00:41:42,737 --> 00:41:43,737
Okay.

710
00:41:43,738 --> 00:41:45,636
I want to add a voice,

711
00:41:45,637 --> 00:41:47,537
going, "You can do it!"

712
00:41:47,767 --> 00:41:49,476
I want to build it up...

713
00:41:49,477 --> 00:41:51,536
to continue the performance.

714
00:41:51,537 --> 00:41:52,906
The core theme...

715
00:41:52,907 --> 00:41:55,647
uniting my performance is "breath."

716
00:41:55,877 --> 00:41:58,076
Runners need...

717
00:41:58,077 --> 00:42:00,486
a steady rhythm of breath to maintain their pace,

718
00:42:00,487 --> 00:42:02,086
just as we dancers need to be in sync,

719
00:42:02,087 --> 00:42:04,616
breathing as one, to execute sharp group choreo.

720
00:42:04,617 --> 00:42:06,056
I brought the marathoner's breath...

721
00:42:06,057 --> 00:42:08,586
shown in the video...

722
00:42:08,587 --> 00:42:11,057
onto the stage through the dancers' breath.

723
00:42:11,457 --> 00:42:13,167
The teaser video ends...

724
00:42:13,367 --> 00:42:15,367
with the runner taking an inhale.

725
00:42:16,167 --> 00:42:17,967
But my performance begins...

726
00:42:19,407 --> 00:42:21,367
with an exhale.

727
00:42:21,767 --> 00:42:23,107
I hope...

728
00:42:23,337 --> 00:42:25,906
my performance makes people feel...

729
00:42:25,907 --> 00:42:28,347
like they can do it.

730
00:42:29,377 --> 00:42:31,946
Marathon runners don't run...

731
00:42:31,947 --> 00:42:33,546
in a straight line like sprinters do.

732
00:42:33,547 --> 00:42:35,586
Creating formations...

733
00:42:35,587 --> 00:42:38,056
that have ups and downs like our lives...

734
00:42:38,057 --> 00:42:40,057
will be more convincing.

735
00:42:40,287 --> 00:42:44,126
Instead of moving the dancers around in a studio,

736
00:42:44,127 --> 00:42:46,166
I try to set the formations first...

737
00:42:46,167 --> 00:42:47,767
in advance.

738
00:42:48,327 --> 00:42:50,697
This way, it's easier to picture it.

739
00:42:51,137 --> 00:42:53,166
I meticulously plan the routes...

740
00:42:53,167 --> 00:42:55,167
and see if the timing is right as I intended...

741
00:42:55,407 --> 00:42:57,876
before practice.

742
00:42:57,877 --> 00:43:00,407
I can prevent the dancers from running into each other.

743
00:43:00,547 --> 00:43:03,316
You're all going to bump into each other.

744
00:43:03,317 --> 00:43:06,917
Koo Young, this part is the problem. Trix goes this way.

745
00:43:07,687 --> 00:43:09,387
KNUCKS goes this way.

746
00:43:09,757 --> 00:43:10,817
Good.

747
00:43:12,017 --> 00:43:15,287
It's an S-shaped formation to describe a road.

748
00:43:15,387 --> 00:43:18,157
You can find your name and follow along.

749
00:43:18,327 --> 00:43:21,026
You're going to the spots that I just saw you, okay?

750
00:43:21,027 --> 00:43:24,937
One, two, three, four, five,

751
00:43:25,137 --> 00:43:28,037
six, seven, eight.

752
00:43:28,607 --> 00:43:30,437
How did you do that in one go?

753
00:43:30,707 --> 00:43:32,677
(The formation design was 100-percent accurate.)

754
00:43:32,737 --> 00:43:34,607
Okay. I think we're good to go.

755
00:43:35,007 --> 00:43:38,417
I've been dancing...

756
00:43:38,617 --> 00:43:40,287
for a long time now.

757
00:43:40,517 --> 00:43:43,017
In the final performance, I get to show people my dance...

758
00:43:43,117 --> 00:43:44,787
and what I created.

759
00:43:45,057 --> 00:43:49,497
It's an opportunity to leave my name behind in my era.

760
00:43:50,297 --> 00:43:53,297
It's a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

761
00:43:54,497 --> 00:43:57,097
I will show you...

762
00:43:57,397 --> 00:44:00,007
my final work of art...

763
00:44:00,807 --> 00:44:02,637
with my name on it.

764
00:44:05,077 --> 00:44:06,146
(Marathon is a sport...)

765
00:44:06,147 --> 00:44:07,246
(where you run a long way in your own pace.)

766
00:44:07,247 --> 00:44:08,346
(Though they run at different paces, )

767
00:44:08,347 --> 00:44:09,447
(people's support follows.)

768
00:44:11,777 --> 00:44:12,887
Along the way,

769
00:44:13,647 --> 00:44:15,647
there will be countless hurdles.

770
00:44:56,297 --> 00:45:00,127
(Performance by Back Koo Young, "Run Alone, But Never Alone")

771
00:45:33,567 --> 00:45:34,997
This road is long.

772
00:45:36,397 --> 00:45:38,197
It was never meant to be short.

773
00:45:39,567 --> 00:45:40,767
Along the way,

774
00:45:41,337 --> 00:45:43,337
there will be countless hurdles.

775
00:46:27,517 --> 00:46:28,587
You can do it.

776
00:46:30,457 --> 00:46:31,717
You can do it!

777
00:46:34,057 --> 00:46:35,587
You can do it!

778
00:47:43,127 --> 00:47:44,356
(Team Back Koo Young's dancers)

779
00:47:44,357 --> 00:47:45,626
(KNUCKS, Trix, Aiki, Rihey, KCHAN, )

780
00:47:45,627 --> 00:47:47,107
(Seungmin, Lee Na Ra, Kim Yun Won...)

781
00:48:01,377 --> 00:48:02,447
Good job!

782
00:48:15,887 --> 00:48:19,797
Thank you, Director Back Koo Young, for the Cheer Performance Mission.

783
00:48:22,327 --> 00:48:24,736
As shown in the teaser,

784
00:48:24,737 --> 00:48:28,266
the marathoners' unyielding challenge and energy...

785
00:48:28,267 --> 00:48:31,437
were presented as an expanded performance.

786
00:48:33,277 --> 00:48:35,846
Despite the long race where the end was not clear,

787
00:48:35,847 --> 00:48:38,816
the marathoners kept going forward without giving up.

788
00:48:38,817 --> 00:48:41,816
And the moment where they picked up the marathoner on the ground...

789
00:48:41,817 --> 00:48:44,717
and ran toward the finish line together.

790
00:48:45,057 --> 00:48:47,886
Back Koo Young presented the meaning of racing together...

791
00:48:47,887 --> 00:48:50,797
with his directing skills.

792
00:48:53,897 --> 00:48:58,367
How did real marathoners feel about Back Koo Young's performance?

793
00:48:59,167 --> 00:49:01,336
The former national marathoner Kwon Eun Ju...

794
00:49:01,337 --> 00:49:04,407
joined us here today.

795
00:49:06,477 --> 00:49:09,106
Can you share your thoughts...

796
00:49:09,107 --> 00:49:11,517
about the message in his performance?

797
00:49:11,817 --> 00:49:12,846
Hello.

798
00:49:12,847 --> 00:49:17,057
I'm a former national marathoner Kwon Eun Ju.

799
00:49:18,287 --> 00:49:21,126
My heart is pounding...

800
00:49:21,127 --> 00:49:23,596
as if I just did a full marathon.

801
00:49:23,597 --> 00:49:25,596
Actually,

802
00:49:25,597 --> 00:49:29,326
when I stand on the start line,

803
00:49:29,327 --> 00:49:31,136
there's excitement, fear,

804
00:49:31,137 --> 00:49:34,236
and concern...

805
00:49:34,237 --> 00:49:36,106
about whether I'll be able to finish it.

806
00:49:36,107 --> 00:49:39,376
The wait is short, but it feels long.

807
00:49:39,377 --> 00:49:40,746
And I can't wait...

808
00:49:40,747 --> 00:49:44,046
to hear the gunshot and run.

809
00:49:44,047 --> 00:49:45,876
When you began the performance,

810
00:49:45,877 --> 00:49:49,386
I felt the same level of tension.

811
00:49:49,387 --> 00:49:50,856
I recently completed...

812
00:49:50,857 --> 00:49:53,727
the Berlin marathon.

813
00:49:54,287 --> 00:49:56,186
Every time I complete one,

814
00:49:56,187 --> 00:49:59,026
it's exciting at first,

815
00:49:59,027 --> 00:50:00,296
but after I set out,

816
00:50:00,297 --> 00:50:03,126
I also regret...

817
00:50:03,127 --> 00:50:04,727
doing something so hard again and again.

818
00:50:04,897 --> 00:50:08,236
After 5 or 10km,

819
00:50:08,237 --> 00:50:12,406
my breathing becomes stable,

820
00:50:12,407 --> 00:50:14,206
and my pace becomes stable...

821
00:50:14,207 --> 00:50:16,546
as I take each step forward.

822
00:50:16,547 --> 00:50:20,016
Then at 30 or 35km point, my legs cramp up...

823
00:50:20,017 --> 00:50:22,646
or I run out of energy...

824
00:50:22,647 --> 00:50:24,416
that I want to stop.

825
00:50:24,417 --> 00:50:27,726
I just want to lie down.

826
00:50:27,727 --> 00:50:29,786
And he depicted that too.

827
00:50:29,787 --> 00:50:33,667
I felt as if I was running at that moment.

828
00:50:34,227 --> 00:50:35,826
Then at the end,

829
00:50:35,827 --> 00:50:39,266
there was a fanfare after passing the finish line.

830
00:50:39,267 --> 00:50:43,206
The sense of accomplishment and gratitude...

831
00:50:43,207 --> 00:50:47,146
after completing my own race.

832
00:50:47,147 --> 00:50:49,946
I was able to feel them.

833
00:50:49,947 --> 00:50:54,686
It felt like I completed a full marathon today.

834
00:50:54,687 --> 00:50:57,287
I really enjoyed watching. Thank you.

835
00:50:59,417 --> 00:51:01,256
Thanks to the former national marathoner Kwon Eun Ju...

836
00:51:01,257 --> 00:51:03,127
for sharing her thoughts.

837
00:51:03,857 --> 00:51:06,897
This time, I will ask Director Back Koo Young.

838
00:51:07,297 --> 00:51:11,136
After listening to the real marathoner's thoughts,

839
00:51:11,137 --> 00:51:14,807
your sincerity toward the performance feels even deeper.

840
00:51:15,307 --> 00:51:17,876
Do you think it conveyed...

841
00:51:17,877 --> 00:51:20,847
the cheer and the message you wanted to include in this?

842
00:51:23,047 --> 00:51:24,577
Well, yes.

843
00:51:26,887 --> 00:51:29,717
An event like a marathon...

844
00:51:30,417 --> 00:51:31,617
really cheers up...

845
00:51:32,787 --> 00:51:34,887
people like me.

846
00:51:38,057 --> 00:51:40,127
When we dance a lot,

847
00:51:40,967 --> 00:51:45,297
we run out of breath.

848
00:51:45,967 --> 00:51:48,167
The marathoners...

849
00:51:49,007 --> 00:51:52,277
also run at their own pace.

850
00:51:53,747 --> 00:51:57,377
We all have our own pace,

851
00:51:58,347 --> 00:52:02,046
and I wanted to show...

852
00:52:02,047 --> 00:52:04,917
how that becomes one...

853
00:52:05,617 --> 00:52:07,256
in the film and the performance.

854
00:52:07,257 --> 00:52:10,026
I also wanted to...

855
00:52:10,027 --> 00:52:12,197
comfort people...

856
00:52:12,657 --> 00:52:14,367
more than how a marathon...

857
00:52:15,597 --> 00:52:17,537
comforted me.

858
00:52:18,137 --> 00:52:22,837
If it comforted you even a little, I'd be more than grateful.

859
00:52:25,437 --> 00:52:28,706
We've listened to his directing purpose.

860
00:52:28,707 --> 00:52:31,977
This time, we'll listen to the Fight Judges.

861
00:52:32,547 --> 00:52:34,516
His performance conveyed the unyielding challenge...

862
00:52:34,517 --> 00:52:38,257
and support for each other.

863
00:52:38,687 --> 00:52:41,086
Honey J,

864
00:52:41,087 --> 00:52:43,426
what did you think of his message about challenge and cheer...

865
00:52:43,427 --> 00:52:46,327
he conveyed through a marathon?

866
00:52:47,627 --> 00:52:51,437
First of all, congratulations on completing your race.

867
00:52:51,737 --> 00:52:52,897
Congratulations.

868
00:52:56,067 --> 00:52:59,407
Should I say...

869
00:52:59,807 --> 00:53:01,287
Director Back Koo Young always has...

870
00:53:01,807 --> 00:53:04,877
a good story?

871
00:53:05,617 --> 00:53:09,616
When a topic is given,

872
00:53:09,617 --> 00:53:12,587
everyone has a different way of describing it.

873
00:53:12,957 --> 00:53:16,656
Director Back Koo Young especially...

874
00:53:16,657 --> 00:53:18,696
has outstanding skills to deliver the message...

875
00:53:18,697 --> 00:53:22,626
and to direct the story.

876
00:53:22,627 --> 00:53:26,196
I've always admired that about him.

877
00:53:26,197 --> 00:53:27,967
Today, once again,

878
00:53:29,007 --> 00:53:32,977
I want to thank him...

879
00:53:34,107 --> 00:53:38,477
for delivering such an overwhelming message.

880
00:53:39,717 --> 00:53:42,946
I think he has amazing directing skills...

881
00:53:42,947 --> 00:53:45,757
to make good use of many dancers.

882
00:53:46,117 --> 00:53:49,057
Once again today, he used many dancers...

883
00:53:49,427 --> 00:53:52,356
cleverly...

884
00:53:52,357 --> 00:53:55,466
and wisely.

885
00:53:55,467 --> 00:53:57,837
I give him credit for that.

886
00:53:59,867 --> 00:54:01,736
He keeps good balance...

887
00:54:01,737 --> 00:54:03,607
between artistic quality and mass appeal.

888
00:54:04,177 --> 00:54:06,976
He always creates a performance...

889
00:54:06,977 --> 00:54:11,417
that many people can relate to.

890
00:54:11,547 --> 00:54:15,047
That's also very amazing.

891
00:54:15,487 --> 00:54:19,487
In terms of a message,

892
00:54:20,527 --> 00:54:23,126
it was very touching.

893
00:54:23,127 --> 00:54:26,967
As you said earlier,

894
00:54:27,597 --> 00:54:29,727
life is a marathon.

895
00:54:30,267 --> 00:54:34,107
This performance wasn't just for marathoners,

896
00:54:34,237 --> 00:54:36,166
but for everyone...

897
00:54:36,167 --> 00:54:39,406
who is sometimes exhausted...

898
00:54:39,407 --> 00:54:43,206
living this era.

899
00:54:43,207 --> 00:54:45,176
I believe it was a message for all of us.

900
00:54:45,177 --> 00:54:48,546
Thank you for creating a performance...

901
00:54:48,547 --> 00:54:51,117
that will cheer us up when we are down.

902
00:54:55,827 --> 00:54:58,997
Thanks to Honey J for her comment.

903
00:54:59,327 --> 00:55:02,396
Director Back Koo Young completed...

904
00:55:02,397 --> 00:55:05,196
a teaser and a live performance...

905
00:55:05,197 --> 00:55:07,067
with a marathon as a topic.

906
00:55:07,837 --> 00:55:10,106
And now, how much did the global public judges...

907
00:55:10,107 --> 00:55:13,106
support the teaser...

908
00:55:13,107 --> 00:55:15,777
that was revealed previously?

909
00:55:16,707 --> 00:55:19,546
Here is the result of the online pre-voting...

910
00:55:19,547 --> 00:55:21,447
that takes up 30 percent of the final score...

911
00:55:21,747 --> 00:55:25,357
and the number of likes.

912
00:56:09,127 --> 00:56:11,266
For the Cheer Performance video,

913
00:56:11,267 --> 00:56:14,036
the number of likes he received...

914
00:56:14,037 --> 00:56:16,906
is 24,928.

915
00:56:16,907 --> 00:56:18,737
(24,928 likes)

916
00:56:22,707 --> 00:56:24,976
Since Back Koo Young received...

917
00:56:24,977 --> 00:56:27,246
almost double BADA's number of likes,

918
00:56:27,247 --> 00:56:31,356
he is ahead of her in terms of online pre-voting.

919
00:56:31,357 --> 00:56:35,687
Will he be able to keep this going to the end?

920
00:56:37,827 --> 00:56:41,126
The live voting that takes up 70 percent of the final score...

921
00:56:41,127 --> 00:56:45,197
will take place after all four directors finish performing.

922
00:56:45,837 --> 00:56:49,766
We ask the viewers to remember...

923
00:56:49,767 --> 00:56:53,576
how much his live performance today...

924
00:56:53,577 --> 00:56:56,276
incorporated the performance he foreshadowed in the teaser.

925
00:56:56,277 --> 00:56:58,476
And please support him...

926
00:56:58,477 --> 00:57:00,687
in the live voting that will soon take place.

927
00:57:05,487 --> 00:57:07,656
That is all for Director Back Koo Young.

928
00:57:07,657 --> 00:57:10,227
Thank you for your performance.

929
00:57:13,057 --> 00:57:16,567
Please give it up for Back Koo Young for his wonderful performance.

930
00:57:27,207 --> 00:57:29,546
The final Cheer Performance Mission.

931
00:57:29,547 --> 00:57:31,817
The next director to perform is...

932
00:57:33,747 --> 00:57:35,247
BABYZOO.

933
00:57:40,827 --> 00:57:43,226
From battles to K-pop choreography,

934
00:57:43,227 --> 00:57:46,356
the all-rounder director BABYZOO demonstrated his unique skills...

935
00:57:46,357 --> 00:57:48,397
by moving across a diverse range of genres.

936
00:57:48,827 --> 00:57:50,066
In Street World Fighter,

937
00:57:50,067 --> 00:57:52,866
based on his wide range of experience and detailed directing,

938
00:57:52,867 --> 00:57:56,107
he proved he was worthy of his nickname as an all-rounder.

939
00:57:57,977 --> 00:58:01,447
After numerous challenges, he's finally reached the final.

940
00:58:01,707 --> 00:58:04,577
The sport Director BABYZOO chose is...

941
00:58:05,017 --> 00:58:06,047
fencing.

942
00:58:07,017 --> 00:58:10,587
In the teaser video released, Director BABYZOO captured...

943
00:58:10,787 --> 00:58:13,257
the signature tension of fencing...

944
00:58:13,357 --> 00:58:14,656
through a minor clash in everyday life...

945
00:58:14,657 --> 00:58:16,227
escalating into an intense showdown.

946
00:58:16,927 --> 00:58:20,667
How has Director BABYZOO completed these extremely tense moments...

947
00:58:20,767 --> 00:58:23,227
through his performance?

948
00:58:24,097 --> 00:58:27,337
Director BABYZOO's Cheer Performance Mission.

949
00:58:27,437 --> 00:58:29,467
It begins now.

950
00:58:31,477 --> 00:58:33,707
Ready, fight!

951
00:58:34,547 --> 00:58:37,147
(Credit Board, BABYZOO)

952
00:58:37,577 --> 00:58:39,516
Hi, everyone.

953
00:58:39,517 --> 00:58:42,986
I made the final!

954
00:58:42,987 --> 00:58:43,987
(BABYZOO makes the final.)

955
00:58:43,988 --> 00:58:45,756
The final is just around the corner.

956
00:58:45,757 --> 00:58:47,626
I'd like to thank you all in advance.

957
00:58:47,627 --> 00:58:49,156
The reason you're here today is...

958
00:58:49,157 --> 00:58:51,956
that the final mission is the Cheer Performance Mission.

959
00:58:51,957 --> 00:58:55,466
I chose fencing.

960
00:58:55,467 --> 00:58:56,726
I thought fencing was...

961
00:58:56,727 --> 00:58:59,036
very similar to my battles.

962
00:58:59,037 --> 00:59:00,666
During the 1-on-1 battle,

963
00:59:00,667 --> 00:59:02,166
the moment I catch my opponent's weakness,

964
00:59:02,167 --> 00:59:04,136
it requires a high level of concentration to go for it.

965
00:59:04,137 --> 00:59:05,536
I thought that was similar to fencing.

966
00:59:05,537 --> 00:59:07,646
I instantly wanted to...

967
00:59:07,647 --> 00:59:08,776
demonstrate that on stage.

968
00:59:08,777 --> 00:59:10,716
I put a lot of thought into it.

969
00:59:10,717 --> 00:59:12,246
While thinking,

970
00:59:12,247 --> 00:59:15,546
I realized I represented Korea.

971
00:59:15,547 --> 00:59:19,256
When it's a draw,

972
00:59:19,257 --> 00:59:21,056
the thrill of winning one more point.

973
00:59:21,057 --> 00:59:22,986
I thought about the moment when victory...

974
00:59:22,987 --> 00:59:25,196
brings everyone together.

975
00:59:25,197 --> 00:59:27,626
Let me tell you about the mood first.

976
00:59:27,627 --> 00:59:30,866
We win by one point.

977
00:59:30,867 --> 00:59:34,607
The struggle to win a point.

978
00:59:34,707 --> 00:59:37,976
My goal is to include that...

979
00:59:37,977 --> 00:59:40,106
in my final performance.

980
00:59:40,107 --> 00:59:41,346
Since we're Team Korea,

981
00:59:41,347 --> 00:59:43,846
I want the traditional Korean sound...

982
00:59:43,847 --> 00:59:45,277
but with a sense of rhythm.

983
00:59:45,547 --> 00:59:48,586
Since this is about...

984
00:59:48,587 --> 00:59:50,116
cheering up national athletes,

985
00:59:50,117 --> 00:59:51,816
I thought the traditional Korean sound...

986
00:59:51,817 --> 00:59:54,626
would make them feel...

987
00:59:54,627 --> 00:59:56,756
supportive.

988
00:59:56,757 --> 00:59:58,796
That's why I decided to add that in the beginning.

989
00:59:58,797 --> 01:00:01,366
Personally, I like that composition.

990
01:00:01,367 --> 01:00:03,966
I'll follow the composition in the beginning.

991
01:00:03,967 --> 01:00:06,136
But if I focus too much on the Korean sound,

992
01:00:06,137 --> 01:00:07,636
it'll be too classical.

993
01:00:07,637 --> 01:00:09,906
Let's mix...

994
01:00:09,907 --> 01:00:12,737
classic with the modern sound.

995
01:00:12,837 --> 01:00:15,406
I plan to build a structure...

996
01:00:15,407 --> 01:00:18,247
where the festival starts near the end.

997
01:00:18,447 --> 01:00:20,787
I want you...

998
01:00:20,887 --> 01:00:24,516
to cheer physically.

999
01:00:24,517 --> 01:00:26,456
The dancers will dance as a group...

1000
01:00:26,457 --> 01:00:29,627
to make it look like an opening ceremony.

1001
01:00:30,387 --> 01:00:32,426
Two, three, four,

1002
01:00:32,427 --> 01:00:33,826
five, six...

1003
01:00:33,827 --> 01:00:36,396
I like a variety...

1004
01:00:36,397 --> 01:00:37,996
of solid scenes.

1005
01:00:37,997 --> 01:00:40,366
I decided to push it...

1006
01:00:40,367 --> 01:00:41,906
and incorporate diverse structures.

1007
01:00:41,907 --> 01:00:44,306
I also wanted to send them a cheer...

1008
01:00:44,307 --> 01:00:46,676
by presenting a thrill...

1009
01:00:46,677 --> 01:00:48,176
from a perfectly sharp group choreography.

1010
01:00:48,177 --> 01:00:51,217
I added tutting.

1011
01:00:51,317 --> 01:00:53,917
Go.

1012
01:00:54,017 --> 01:00:55,986
My voice goes,

1013
01:00:55,987 --> 01:00:57,416
"Bob, bob, ah, ah."

1014
01:00:57,417 --> 01:00:59,656
So make sure to stop after every beat.

1015
01:00:59,657 --> 01:01:01,326
- Okay. - Yes.

1016
01:01:01,327 --> 01:01:02,956
And I have a secret weapon.

1017
01:01:02,957 --> 01:01:04,026
Hello.

1018
01:01:04,027 --> 01:01:06,396
I'm Kang Gyeong Ho from "Stage Fighter."

1019
01:01:06,397 --> 01:01:07,726
(Exclaiming)

1020
01:01:07,727 --> 01:01:10,226
I needed Gyeong Ho for the final performance...

1021
01:01:10,227 --> 01:01:13,196
because I needed the ballet technique, the lines,

1022
01:01:13,197 --> 01:01:16,337
and his powerful energy.

1023
01:01:16,437 --> 01:01:19,476
I thought we'd make good harmony.

1024
01:01:19,477 --> 01:01:21,906
It'll look great...

1025
01:01:21,907 --> 01:01:24,576
if we mix it up with fencing.

1026
01:01:24,577 --> 01:01:27,286
So I prepared these!

1027
01:01:27,287 --> 01:01:28,546
(He prepared real fencing swords.)

1028
01:01:28,547 --> 01:01:29,547
(Flustered)

1029
01:01:29,548 --> 01:01:30,557
(I'm not doing ballet?)

1030
01:01:30,657 --> 01:01:33,186
Show the fierce look in your eyes. Clang.

1031
01:01:33,187 --> 01:01:35,656
This is going to be...

1032
01:01:35,657 --> 01:01:37,156
a tense, yet restrained...

1033
01:01:37,157 --> 01:01:39,126
and dynamic performance...

1034
01:01:39,127 --> 01:01:42,127
where the condensed energy explodes.

1035
01:01:42,427 --> 01:01:43,526
My feet got so dirty.

1036
01:01:43,527 --> 01:01:46,196
Exactly. That proves our passion.

1037
01:01:46,197 --> 01:01:49,136
I never learned fencing or know how to mimic it.

1038
01:01:49,137 --> 01:01:51,476
But it reflects my admiration...

1039
01:01:51,477 --> 01:01:53,136
and affection toward the fencers.

1040
01:01:53,137 --> 01:01:55,476
I hope the national athletes...

1041
01:01:55,477 --> 01:01:56,776
find this as a gift.

1042
01:01:56,777 --> 01:01:59,147
- Let's do our best to the end. - Let's go.

1043
01:01:59,717 --> 01:02:01,186
Shall we practice?

1044
01:02:01,187 --> 01:02:02,846
And to be honest,

1045
01:02:02,847 --> 01:02:06,357
I don't have much experience as a director yet.

1046
01:02:06,457 --> 01:02:08,686
(During the preliminary interview)

1047
01:02:08,687 --> 01:02:11,096
I was different from others from the start.

1048
01:02:11,097 --> 01:02:13,027
I took longer than others.

1049
01:02:13,897 --> 01:02:16,466
I believe I was underperforming in the beginning.

1050
01:02:16,467 --> 01:02:19,137
(He started off as the worst candidate.)

1051
01:02:19,237 --> 01:02:20,337
(Bitter)

1052
01:02:20,707 --> 01:02:24,177
(BABYZOO ended up going to the Last Stage.)

1053
01:02:24,277 --> 01:02:26,877
(I'm not sure about myself.)

1054
01:02:27,807 --> 01:02:29,706
(What's wrong with me?)

1055
01:02:29,707 --> 01:02:31,877
Yet I did my best.

1056
01:02:31,977 --> 01:02:34,486
(As a unique player on stage...)

1057
01:02:34,487 --> 01:02:37,317
(and a through director who never misses even minor details, )

1058
01:02:37,417 --> 01:02:39,416
(BABYZOO did his best every moment.)

1059
01:02:39,417 --> 01:02:42,626
A lot of people know me...

1060
01:02:42,627 --> 01:02:44,296
as a battler,

1061
01:02:44,297 --> 01:02:46,396
but through this show,

1062
01:02:46,397 --> 01:02:48,826
I want to establish myself as a director and a choreographer.

1063
01:02:48,827 --> 01:02:51,536
It'll be even better if I get a good result.

1064
01:02:51,537 --> 01:02:52,836
I'm going to win.

1065
01:02:52,837 --> 01:02:54,537
Who else is going to win other than me?

1066
01:02:55,737 --> 01:02:58,576
Since many people supported me and helped me,

1067
01:02:58,577 --> 01:03:00,106
I will create a performance...

1068
01:03:00,107 --> 01:03:03,307
that I like without any regrets.

1069
01:03:03,407 --> 01:03:05,046
("En Garde")

1070
01:03:05,047 --> 01:03:06,676
(As a Korean fencer, one athlete carries the weight...)

1071
01:03:06,677 --> 01:03:08,957
(of the responsibility and expectations placed upon him.)

1072
01:03:49,527 --> 01:03:51,756
(Performance by BABYZOO)

1073
01:03:51,757 --> 01:03:54,027
("En Garde" Produced by THE HUB)

1074
01:06:23,607 --> 01:06:24,876
(Team BABYZOO's dancers)

1075
01:06:24,877 --> 01:06:26,076
(Kang Gyeong Ho, Jeong Eun Seol, Dahye, Pyeong Ga, CHAEYEON)

1076
01:06:26,077 --> 01:06:27,316
