1337
01:19:08,007 --> 01:19:09,476
(I'm going to live if I'm ready to die.)

1338
01:19:09,477 --> 01:19:10,946
(I'm going to die if I try to live.)

1339
01:19:10,947 --> 01:19:13,647
(I'm going to be ready to die.)

1340
01:19:14,147 --> 01:19:16,947
"Let's fight until the end while I'm here." This was my mindset.

1341
01:19:17,317 --> 01:19:18,587
With that mindset,

1342
01:19:18,787 --> 01:19:20,917
the failures I went through...

1343
01:19:21,217 --> 01:19:23,257
became a strong foothold.

1344
01:19:23,427 --> 01:19:25,996
I believe this is the right time...

1345
01:19:25,997 --> 01:19:28,597
to leap up with that foothold.

1346
01:19:28,927 --> 01:19:30,997
This is the last performance...

1347
01:19:31,227 --> 01:19:33,766
and I wish to make everyone say,

1348
01:19:33,767 --> 01:19:35,407
"Kasper is a director."

1349
01:19:36,137 --> 01:19:40,207
I wish to put together a performance with everything I have.

1350
01:19:41,407 --> 01:19:42,646
(SHUTDOWN: The Final Fight, Kasper)

1351
01:19:42,647 --> 01:19:43,806
(Synopsis: The Trojan Horse takes over the valley.)

1352
01:19:43,807 --> 01:19:45,116
(The savior and controller takes a step in the battlefield.)

1353
01:19:45,117 --> 01:19:47,437
(A great explosion occurs as the shackles are broken off.)

1354
01:20:25,957 --> 01:20:30,227
("Trojan Horse" by BAEKHYUN Performance by Kasper)

1355
01:23:26,797 --> 01:23:27,797
(Team Kasper Dancer: Shuri, Lim Ji Hyun, Minsoo, Kim Ye Hwan, )

1356
01:23:27,798 --> 01:23:28,866
(Kim Ye Hwan, Suzy Hong, Dora, Lee Kyung Woo, Ruizen, Nino, )

1357
01:23:28,867 --> 01:23:29,906
(Jung So Won, Kim Ye Rin, docobi, Jung Yoo Min, Cho Yeon Kyung, )

1358
01:23:29,907 --> 01:23:32,187
(Kim Yeo Min, Kim Bo Won, Ain, kemes, verre, Dansy, RUFF)

1359
01:23:41,617 --> 01:23:45,217
That was Director Kasper's Cheer Performance Mission.

1360
01:23:46,257 --> 01:23:48,756
With his experience of directing the opening...

1361
01:23:48,757 --> 01:23:50,557
for the League of Legends World Championship,

1362
01:23:50,687 --> 01:23:51,996
he expressed the game universe...

1363
01:23:51,997 --> 01:23:54,097
through his performance.

1364
01:23:54,457 --> 01:23:56,227
An intense competition of strategies...

1365
01:23:56,297 --> 01:23:58,327
and the teamwork between teammates.

1366
01:23:58,867 --> 01:24:01,567
The game characters were expressed through the performance...

1367
01:24:01,767 --> 01:24:05,007
and various stage effects such as the lights and fog were used.

1368
01:24:05,337 --> 01:24:07,737
The dynamic energy of E-sports...

1369
01:24:07,907 --> 01:24:10,707
was expressed by Kasper's directing skills.

1370
01:24:12,677 --> 01:24:14,917
How did an actual E-sports player...

1371
01:24:15,047 --> 01:24:18,217
feel about this performance?

1372
01:24:18,917 --> 01:24:21,186
Today, we have E-sports coach Yoon Sang Hoon...

1373
01:24:21,187 --> 01:24:23,427
as a special guest.

1374
01:24:24,227 --> 01:24:26,627
E-sports was expressed by Kasper's performance...

1375
01:24:26,727 --> 01:24:29,366
with a message of support.

1376
01:24:29,367 --> 01:24:31,167
I'm curious to know how you felt about it.

1377
01:24:32,497 --> 01:24:33,566
Hello.

1378
01:24:33,567 --> 01:24:37,906
I'm the national team coach of Korea's E-sports team.

1379
01:24:37,907 --> 01:24:39,277
My name is Yoon Sang Hoon.

1380
01:24:41,077 --> 01:24:42,177
First of all,

1381
01:24:43,107 --> 01:24:45,276
I was very curious...

1382
01:24:45,277 --> 01:24:47,816
about how he would express E-sports through his performance.

1383
01:24:47,817 --> 01:24:49,947
After watching the teaser,

1384
01:24:50,217 --> 01:24:54,257
I wondered what kind of performance he would put together.

1385
01:24:54,417 --> 01:24:57,287
I really enjoyed the amazing performance.

1386
01:24:57,727 --> 01:25:00,897
This was what I felt while watching the performance.

1387
01:25:02,027 --> 01:25:04,567
It's the same with every kind of sport.

1388
01:25:04,727 --> 01:25:06,567
There are winners and losers.

1389
01:25:06,837 --> 01:25:08,736
It was the last team fight.

1390
01:25:08,737 --> 01:25:11,566
The winners stood out in that scene,

1391
01:25:11,567 --> 01:25:13,453
but it was a reminder that they were able to shine...

1392
01:25:13,477 --> 01:25:16,347
thanks to the losers.

1393
01:25:18,207 --> 01:25:22,646
It was a performance that all E-sports players would enjoy...

1394
01:25:22,647 --> 01:25:25,286
and it was a great message of support.

1395
01:25:25,287 --> 01:25:26,317
Thank you.

1396
01:25:28,287 --> 01:25:31,427
That was Yoon Sang Hoon, the E-sports coach.

1397
01:25:31,827 --> 01:25:34,497
I will ask Director Kasper this time.

1398
01:25:34,927 --> 01:25:37,466
After hearing from Coach Yoon Sang Hoon,

1399
01:25:37,467 --> 01:25:39,736
the message of today's performance...

1400
01:25:39,737 --> 01:25:41,267
felt a lot clearer.

1401
01:25:41,597 --> 01:25:44,566
Do you believe the idea of your performance...

1402
01:25:44,567 --> 01:25:48,037
was expressed well during today's performance?

1403
01:25:49,707 --> 01:25:53,347
While preparing for this E-sports performance,

1404
01:25:54,117 --> 01:25:56,646
I designed the start as an introduction to the characters.

1405
01:25:56,647 --> 01:25:59,856
He mentioned the last team fight. I thought really hard...

1406
01:25:59,857 --> 01:26:02,427
about how to express this based on the 5-on-5 battle.

1407
01:26:02,687 --> 01:26:04,626
I've spent a lot of time...

1408
01:26:04,627 --> 01:26:06,527
on how to express the sense of victory.

1409
01:26:06,957 --> 01:26:08,926
He was able to notice that...

1410
01:26:08,927 --> 01:26:12,837
and it feels like I've done well to express that moment.

1411
01:26:13,437 --> 01:26:16,336
I'm a lover of E-sports myself and I respect it a lot.

1412
01:26:16,337 --> 01:26:21,107
I spend a lot of time gaming as a hobby.

1413
01:26:21,437 --> 01:26:23,647
E-sports was the best choice I could make...

1414
01:26:24,177 --> 01:26:26,676
for this mission.

1415
01:26:26,677 --> 01:26:29,117
That was what led to this performance.

1416
01:26:32,417 --> 01:26:33,517
Thank you.

1417
01:26:33,617 --> 01:26:36,427
Let's hear from the Fight Judges as well.

1418
01:26:36,687 --> 01:26:38,526
The game characters and the game universe...

1419
01:26:38,527 --> 01:26:41,627
were expressed through the amazing live performance.

1420
01:26:42,027 --> 01:26:44,926
Special Judge Ian Eastwood,

1421
01:26:44,927 --> 01:26:47,937
what did you think of Kasper's directing skills...

1422
01:26:48,067 --> 01:26:50,707
based on his live performance of E-sports?

1423
01:26:52,607 --> 01:26:57,576
Well, I had the pleasure of having gotten to dance with Kasper...

1424
01:26:57,577 --> 01:27:00,147
very early on in our dance journey...

1425
01:27:00,547 --> 01:27:02,746
which is really cool.

1426
01:27:02,747 --> 01:27:05,756
But that being said, I was also curious...

1427
01:27:05,757 --> 01:27:08,516
about how you were going to bring E-sports to life.

1428
01:27:08,517 --> 01:27:11,087
As choreographers and directors,

1429
01:27:11,357 --> 01:27:14,756
we're confronted with challenges all the time...

1430
01:27:14,757 --> 01:27:17,627
that we might not know how we're going to conquer.

1431
01:27:17,927 --> 01:27:22,067
And it's one thing as you ascend through the dance industry...

1432
01:27:22,337 --> 01:27:24,266
and dance in general...

1433
01:27:24,267 --> 01:27:28,106
to build your skill and be able to choreograph pieces of choreography.

1434
01:27:28,107 --> 01:27:31,647
But it's another thing to bring concepts to life...

1435
01:27:31,847 --> 01:27:33,876
and push through challenges...

1436
01:27:33,877 --> 01:27:36,647
that are really unique and specific.

1437
01:27:37,047 --> 01:27:39,786
And I just hope you're really proud of yourself, bro.

1438
01:27:39,787 --> 01:27:43,556
Because this was incredibly cinematic.

1439
01:27:43,557 --> 01:27:46,426
And it goes way beyond just being able to do four-eight counts,

1440
01:27:46,427 --> 01:27:49,026
eight-eight counts, and breakdowns...

1441
01:27:49,027 --> 01:27:51,326
that people are very used to seeing in music videos.

1442
01:27:51,327 --> 01:27:52,767
This was a cinematic...

1443
01:27:53,537 --> 01:27:56,307
masterpiece that you've brought to the stage.

1444
01:27:56,367 --> 01:27:58,206
And I just hope you walk away really proud.

1445
01:27:58,207 --> 01:28:00,037
You've come all the way to the final.

1446
01:28:00,237 --> 01:28:01,377
And it's not easy...

1447
01:28:01,607 --> 01:28:05,347
And I just congratulate you, man. Great work.

1448
01:28:08,117 --> 01:28:11,987
Yes. That was the special judge Ian Eastwood.

1449
01:28:12,387 --> 01:28:15,886
Director Kasper crafted a cohesive performance...

1450
01:28:15,887 --> 01:28:18,756
centered on the theme of e-sports, spanning everything...

1451
01:28:18,757 --> 01:28:21,296
from the teaser video to today's live stage.

1452
01:28:21,297 --> 01:28:23,726
Just how enthusiastic was the support...

1453
01:28:23,727 --> 01:28:26,666
from global public judges for the teaser video...

1454
01:28:26,667 --> 01:28:29,637
of Kasper that was unveiled earlier?

1455
01:28:30,307 --> 01:28:33,136
Among the three directors revealed so far,

1456
01:28:33,137 --> 01:28:35,376
Back Koo Young ranks first in terms of the number of "likes,"

1457
01:28:35,377 --> 01:28:38,647
followed by BABYZOO in second place, and BADA in third.

1458
01:28:40,147 --> 01:28:44,447
Will Kasper be able to surpass the records of the three directors?

1459
01:28:45,087 --> 01:28:48,116
I'll reveal the number of likes that Director Kasper...

1460
01:28:48,117 --> 01:28:50,487
