01:45:48,477 --> 01:45:49,906
You can vote through the app, Mnet Plus,

1858
01:45:49,907 --> 01:45:51,777
during the live final broadcast.

1859
01:45:51,977 --> 01:45:54,947
You can also vote by texting hashtag 0011...

1860
01:45:55,047 --> 01:45:56,947
during the live final broadcast.

1861
01:45:57,147 --> 01:45:59,116
Please write down the name or designated number...

1862
01:45:59,117 --> 01:46:01,087
of the director you'd like to support.

1863
01:46:07,557 --> 01:46:09,626
To name the winning director...

1864
01:46:09,627 --> 01:46:11,497
of Street World Fighter: Directors' War,

1865
01:46:11,597 --> 01:46:13,797
the live voting is ongoing now.

1866
01:46:14,067 --> 01:46:18,467
Up next, to turn up the heat for the finals, we have prepared...

1867
01:46:19,907 --> 01:46:21,307
the Special Stage.

1868
01:46:28,477 --> 01:46:31,316
Today, you will get to watch performances...

1869
01:46:31,317 --> 01:46:32,717
from three special teams.

1870
01:46:33,087 --> 01:46:35,257
The first Special Stage is...

1871
01:46:35,357 --> 01:46:38,887
prepared by the crew led by Hash.

1872
01:46:39,687 --> 01:46:43,626
Coming up shortly, COME HERE, the crew who reached the finals...

1873
01:46:43,627 --> 01:46:46,127
on the global competition TV show,

1874
01:46:46,227 --> 01:46:49,037
"America's Got Talent," will take the stage.

1875
01:46:52,707 --> 01:46:54,977
The second Special Stage is...

1876
01:46:55,077 --> 01:46:58,207
led by the crew Director JEONG MIN JUN is part of.

1877
01:46:59,777 --> 01:47:01,876
The crew is a two-time winner...

1878
01:47:01,877 --> 01:47:03,446
of the VIBE Dance Competition,

1879
01:47:03,447 --> 01:47:05,207
a global performance contest held in the US.

1880
01:47:05,317 --> 01:47:06,956
The crew led by Kalvin, The Stories,

1881
01:47:06,957 --> 01:47:09,287
is ready to deliver a performance.

1882
01:47:12,887 --> 01:47:15,526
As for the last Special Stage,

1883
01:47:15,527 --> 01:47:19,026
it features the team that garnered the most attention this season.

1884
01:47:19,027 --> 01:47:20,566
(Super Kids Dancers will put on a special performance shortly.)

1885
01:47:20,567 --> 01:47:23,236
It's the team of Super Kids Dancers.

1886
01:47:23,237 --> 01:47:27,577
(Super Kids Dancers will put on a special performance shortly.)

1887
01:47:28,437 --> 01:47:30,276
During the Super Kids Direct Mission,

1888
01:47:30,277 --> 01:47:32,606
Kids Dancers demonstrated amazing dancing skills...

1889
01:47:32,607 --> 01:47:33,917
and crazy energy.

1890
01:47:34,047 --> 01:47:36,717
The viewers got to watch their performance through the films.

1891
01:47:36,817 --> 01:47:39,246
But today, the viewers can watch their performance live...

1892
01:47:39,247 --> 01:47:41,557
during the final Special Stage.

1893
01:47:42,417 --> 01:47:43,456
All right.

1894
01:47:43,457 --> 01:47:45,787
Let us now watch the special performances...

1895
01:47:45,887 --> 01:47:47,927
prepared by these three teams.

1896
01:47:49,727 --> 01:47:50,967
Ready,

1897
01:47:51,397 --> 01:47:52,567
fight!

1898
01:53:34,037 --> 01:53:35,976
- Have you been well? - Hello.

1899
01:53:35,977 --> 01:53:37,046
(Super Kids and BABYZOO meet after a long time.)

1900
01:53:37,047 --> 01:53:38,246
- That's cool. - You guys said nice things...

1901
01:53:38,247 --> 01:53:39,447
about me.

1902
01:53:39,507 --> 01:53:40,846
BABYZOO is much more handsome...

1903
01:53:40,847 --> 01:53:42,177
- than my dad. - Much more.

1904
01:53:42,217 --> 01:53:43,376
You're 1,000 times more handsome...

1905
01:53:43,377 --> 01:53:44,546
- than my dad. - Yes, you said that.

1906
01:53:44,547 --> 01:53:45,786
- I feel so reassured. - My dad...

1907
01:53:45,787 --> 01:53:47,457
You've gotten more handsome now.

1908
01:53:47,757 --> 01:53:49,186
- Hello! - Hello!

1909
01:53:49,187 --> 01:53:51,387
- Hello. - I'm the first one.

1910
01:53:51,457 --> 01:53:52,827
Yurichika.

1911
01:53:53,087 --> 01:53:55,257
(Not showing any reaction)

1912
01:53:56,197 --> 01:53:58,326
(Are you for real?)

1913
01:53:58,327 --> 01:54:00,367
(She's shy to meet him after a long while.)

1914
01:54:00,697 --> 01:54:01,837
Did you watch the video?

1915
01:54:02,097 --> 01:54:03,167
I did.

1916
01:54:03,267 --> 01:54:04,406
It was amazing.

1917
01:54:04,407 --> 01:54:06,037
I won thanks to you guys.

1918
01:54:06,467 --> 01:54:07,907
(Feeling proud)

1919
01:54:08,237 --> 01:54:09,637
When did you get here?

1920
01:54:10,137 --> 01:54:11,906
- She was so happy. - Really?

1921
01:54:11,907 --> 01:54:13,006
(She was so happy when she got the call.)

1922
01:54:13,007 --> 01:54:14,317
Tell her I'm happy too.

1923
01:54:14,417 --> 01:54:15,717
ShiN.

1924
01:54:15,847 --> 01:54:17,416
She came all the way to Korea.

1925
01:54:17,417 --> 01:54:18,546
I was happy to see everyone again.

1926
01:54:18,547 --> 01:54:20,187
It was like my soul was getting cleansed.

1927
01:54:21,157 --> 01:54:22,256
Director BADA...

1928
01:54:22,257 --> 01:54:24,087
is the only 1 left from the 4-person team.

1929
01:54:24,527 --> 01:54:25,786
Right.

1930
01:54:25,787 --> 01:54:26,787
(Eliminated)

1931
01:54:26,788 --> 01:54:28,696
(They're upset that their directors got eliminated.)

1932
01:54:28,697 --> 01:54:29,896
But...

1933
01:54:29,897 --> 01:54:32,367
Last Stage...

1934
01:54:33,167 --> 01:54:34,196
(Flapping)

1935
01:54:34,197 --> 01:54:35,737
The wings? The Fallen Angel?

1936
01:54:36,097 --> 01:54:37,336
Thank you.

1937
01:54:37,337 --> 01:54:38,837
I missed the kids a lot.

1938
01:54:38,907 --> 01:54:41,376
I still have pictures of them in my phone.

1939
01:54:41,377 --> 01:54:43,777
I look at their pictures when I'm out of energy.

1940
01:54:43,807 --> 01:54:46,446
Actually, now, it will all come down to our stamina...

1941
01:54:46,447 --> 01:54:47,816
when it comes to the finals.

1942
01:54:47,817 --> 01:54:50,046
I could've easily been exhausted.

1943
01:54:50,047 --> 01:54:51,616
But meeting the kids...

1944
01:54:51,617 --> 01:54:53,317
gave me more energy.

1945
01:54:53,687 --> 01:54:55,986
(Why are the directors and Super Kids meeting up?)

1946
01:54:55,987 --> 01:54:58,087
We have to do the outro.

1947
01:54:58,157 --> 01:54:59,887
We'll change it...

1948
01:54:59,927 --> 01:55:01,896
- into the stage version. - Okay.

1949
01:55:01,897 --> 01:55:05,096
In the video, image shots were used for the scenes.

1950
01:55:05,097 --> 01:55:06,097
But this time around,

1951
01:55:06,197 --> 01:55:10,436
the performance needs to flow cohesively from start to finish.

1952
01:55:10,437 --> 01:55:12,166
So we revised the performance...

1953
01:55:12,167 --> 01:55:14,506
by adding more dance moves and new elements.

1954
01:55:14,507 --> 01:55:15,976
During the Super Kids Direct Mission,

1955
01:55:15,977 --> 01:55:18,276
they had to compete against each other.

1956
01:55:18,277 --> 01:55:20,023
But this time around, we're doing a joint performance.

1957
01:55:20,047 --> 01:55:22,246
So we're performing as a team.

1958
01:55:22,247 --> 01:55:24,587
So that will be fun to watch.

1959
01:55:24,647 --> 01:55:27,047
We added an extra solo segment for ShiN.

1960
01:55:27,117 --> 01:55:29,987
We wanted to showcase ShiN more as a dancer.

1961
01:55:30,287 --> 01:55:32,056
We revised the composition of the performance,

1962
01:55:32,057 --> 01:55:33,687
so she could explode on stage once more.

1963
01:55:33,957 --> 01:55:35,903
I thought it'd be a nice way to show her explosive energy.

1964
01:55:35,927 --> 01:55:38,196
In the video, there was a scene...

1965
01:55:38,197 --> 01:55:40,966
where they were rolling around and giggling.

1966
01:55:40,967 --> 01:55:43,436
We could use the bandage in many different ways.

1967
01:55:43,437 --> 01:55:45,113
We wanted to showcase it more to the audience.

1968
01:55:45,137 --> 01:55:47,707
We could make the prop look fancy when they're just...

1969
01:55:47,777 --> 01:55:49,076
goofing around with it.

1970
01:55:49,077 --> 01:55:51,506
I did my best to incorporate that into the performance.

1971
01:55:51,507 --> 01:55:54,716
I'm certain the audience can feel more of the dramatic energy.

1972
01:55:54,717 --> 01:55:57,847
I have no doubt that the Kids Dancers...

1973
01:55:57,947 --> 01:56:00,886
will pour out even more emotions on stage.

1974
01:56:00,887 --> 01:56:03,517
That's definitely something to look forward to.

1975
01:56:03,927 --> 01:56:06,387
(They get to take a break during their practice session.)

1976
01:56:07,197 --> 01:56:08,527
We should get some food.

1977
01:56:08,557 --> 01:56:09,727
I'm hungry.

1978
01:56:09,827 --> 01:56:11,227
(That's why I got this.)

1979
01:56:12,667 --> 01:56:13,667
What was that?

1980
01:56:13,668 --> 01:56:15,813
(Papa Back has been generous and got everyone a snack.)

1981
01:56:15,837 --> 01:56:17,267
(It's the long-awaited snack time!)

1982
01:56:17,407 --> 01:56:18,967
- That looks good. - Yes!

1983
01:56:19,137 --> 01:56:20,336
(We're excited.)

1984
01:56:20,337 --> 01:56:22,076
I got Yurichika and ShiN...

1985
01:56:22,077 --> 01:56:23,376
this lamb sandwich.

1986
01:56:23,377 --> 01:56:24,576
Thank you for the food.

1987
01:56:24,577 --> 01:56:25,607
(Taking a bite)

1988
01:56:25,977 --> 01:56:27,006
(Papa Kasper is satisfied too.)

1989
01:56:27,007 --> 01:56:28,153
- Thank you for the food. - Dig in.

1990
01:56:28,177 --> 01:56:29,247
It's good.

1991
01:56:29,517 --> 01:56:30,787
- It's so good. - Yes.

1992
01:56:30,917 --> 01:56:32,117
- This is very good. - Yes.

1993
01:56:32,187 --> 01:56:34,686
We have to go to specific restaurants to get lamb.

1994
01:56:34,687 --> 01:56:36,286
But we get to eat lamb in a sandwich.

1995
01:56:36,287 --> 01:56:37,486
It's nice and convenient.

1996
01:56:37,487 --> 01:56:39,756
It comes with the herbaceous chimichurri sauce.

1997
01:56:39,757 --> 01:56:41,957
So it doesn't have that gamey flavor you get from lamb.

1998
01:56:42,197 --> 01:56:43,527
What's this, by the way?

1999
01:56:43,967 --> 01:56:44,967
Oh, that?

2000
01:56:44,968 --> 01:56:46,827
That's hummus. It's ground chickpeas.

2001
01:56:46,967 --> 01:56:48,096
So this is hummus.

2002
01:56:48,097 --> 01:56:50,036
Hummus goes well with lamb.

2003
01:56:50,037 --> 01:56:51,136
It's my first time having it.

2004
01:56:51,137 --> 01:56:52,237
It's delicious.

2005
01:56:52,437 --> 01:56:54,706
This is so good that I want to eat 100 of these.

2006
01:56:54,707 --> 01:56:55,707
One hundred again?

2007
01:56:55,708 --> 01:56:57,376
- I want to eat 100 of these. - I want to do it 100 times.

2008
01:56:57,377 --> 01:56:59,483
- I want to eat this again. - Let's try this part again.

2009
01:56:59,507 --> 01:57:01,346
What about you, ShiN and Yurichika?

2010
01:57:01,347 --> 01:57:02,677
- It's so good. - It's so good.

2011
01:57:02,717 --> 01:57:04,847
(How cute.)

2012
01:57:04,987 --> 01:57:06,046
(We did it in Korean.)

2013
01:57:06,047 --> 01:57:08,956
The directors need to do their final stages...

2014
01:57:08,957 --> 01:57:10,586
and the Super Kids Direct Mission.

2015
01:57:10,587 --> 01:57:12,827
Why don't you say something to cheer them on?

2016
01:57:13,087 --> 01:57:14,256
Good luck!

2017
01:57:14,257 --> 01:57:15,257
(Shy)

2018
01:57:16,127 --> 01:57:17,396
Short and strong!

2019
01:57:17,397 --> 01:57:18,526
One, two, three.

2020
01:57:18,527 --> 01:57:20,737
- Let's do this! - Let's do this!

2021
01:57:23,037 --> 01:57:25,036
(Performance by Super Kids)

2022
01:57:25,037 --> 01:57:27,357
("THE MASK: BE YOURSELF and ONWARD," produced by THE HUB)

2023
01:59:28,857 --> 01:59:32,297
(Team Super Kids Stage Dancer)

2024
01:59:39,607 --> 01:59:41,237
The live voting will close.

2025
01:59:42,577 --> 01:59:43,607
Five.

2026
01:59:44,407 --> 01:59:45,447
Four.

2027
01:59:46,577 --> 01:59:47,647
Three.

2028
01:59:48,517 --> 01:59:49,547
Two.

2029
01:59:50,617 --> 01:59:51,647
One.

2030
01:59:52,147 --> 01:59:53,947
The live voting has ended.

2031
01:59:56,087 --> 01:59:57,156
Where's this?

2032
01:59:57,157 --> 01:59:59,626
I came here with my family.

2033
01:59:59,627 --> 02:00:02,427
The view from the top of the building is amazing.

2034
02:00:02,757 --> 02:00:04,296
I don't like high places.

2035
02:00:04,297 --> 02:00:07,067
(Flashback to the thrilling day)

2036
02:00:07,297 --> 02:00:09,966
The view will be amazing at this hour.

2037
02:00:09,967 --> 02:00:12,406
They're treating us so well for the final,

2038
02:00:12,407 --> 02:00:14,207
but I feel rather anxious.

2039
02:00:14,807 --> 02:00:16,276
There must be a reason behind this.

2040
02:00:16,277 --> 02:00:17,376
There must be something.

2041
02:00:17,377 --> 02:00:19,547
- Look at the sky. - Amazing.

2042
02:00:20,477 --> 02:00:21,577
The finalists.

2043
02:00:22,347 --> 02:00:23,547
I'm touched.

2044
02:00:23,577 --> 02:00:25,487
They're welcoming us.

2045
02:00:25,547 --> 02:00:27,486
The view was beautiful.

2046
02:00:27,487 --> 02:00:28,587
It was a surprise gift.

2047
02:00:28,817 --> 02:00:31,227
We can eat while enjoying this view?

2048
02:00:31,887 --> 02:00:33,387
This is so pretty.

2049
02:00:33,987 --> 02:00:36,427
This feels like paradise.

2050
02:00:36,927 --> 02:00:38,296
It's so pretty.

2051
02:00:38,297 --> 02:00:40,227
I feel bad to be here without my wife.

2052
02:00:40,567 --> 02:00:41,637
It looks good.

2053
02:00:42,637 --> 02:00:43,666
I'm so hungry.

2054
02:00:43,667 --> 02:00:45,067
- Thank you. - Thank you.

2055
02:00:45,407 --> 02:00:46,466
- Cheers. - Cheers.

2056
02:00:46,467 --> 02:00:48,136
- Let's do this. - Let's do this.

2057
02:00:48,137 --> 02:00:49,336
(Finalist, Back Koo Young)

2058
02:00:49,337 --> 02:00:50,376
This...

2059
02:00:50,377 --> 02:00:52,547
(Finalists, BABYZOO and BADA)

2060
02:00:52,947 --> 02:00:54,847
(Finalist, Kasper)

2061
02:00:55,177 --> 02:00:56,547
I like Incheon now.

2062
02:00:56,747 --> 02:00:59,247
It was like a comforting gift.

2063
02:00:59,487 --> 02:01:01,957
I get to enjoy such luxury thanks to making it to the final.

2064
02:01:02,987 --> 02:01:04,786
I really wanted to advance to the final.

2065
02:01:04,787 --> 02:01:07,897
I wanted to so desperately.

2066
02:01:09,127 --> 02:01:11,297
Now that I've made it to the final,

2067
02:01:11,627 --> 02:01:13,366
it feels surreal.

2068
02:01:13,367 --> 02:01:17,067
I did think it'd be nice if Tae Woo made it too.

2069
02:01:17,807 --> 02:01:19,507
That was my personal wish.

2070
02:01:19,707 --> 02:01:20,777
- You and I... - Right.

2071
02:01:21,707 --> 02:01:22,877
The boomers.

2072
02:01:23,607 --> 02:01:24,747
Honestly,

2073
02:01:25,147 --> 02:01:28,377
I'm amazed at Koo Young for joining this show.

2074
02:01:29,517 --> 02:01:30,517
(Embarrassed)

2075
02:01:30,517 --> 02:01:31,517
- I'm serious. - Come on.

2076
02:01:31,687 --> 02:01:33,847
He was such a big figure to me when I was young.

2077
02:01:33,987 --> 02:01:37,557
And I really like how he still remains at that position.

2078
02:01:37,687 --> 02:01:39,727
I'm grateful for it.

2079
02:01:40,587 --> 02:01:44,126
I came here after struggling through two Last Stages.

2080
02:01:44,127 --> 02:01:45,496
Two Last Stages...

2081
02:01:45,497 --> 02:01:47,297
Three of us experienced it once.

2082
02:01:47,467 --> 02:01:49,336
The most recent Last Stage was really cool.

2083
02:01:49,337 --> 02:01:50,907
- You did so well. - Really.

2084
02:01:51,367 --> 02:01:52,536
It was incredible.

2085
02:01:52,537 --> 02:01:54,306
It was so well-made.

2086
02:01:54,307 --> 02:01:56,383
(After long struggle for survival, BADA made it to the final.)

2087
02:01:56,407 --> 02:01:58,676
It was the most agonizing days of my life.

2088
02:01:58,677 --> 02:01:59,707
- Really? - Yes.

2089
02:01:59,847 --> 02:02:02,247
I thought you directed it without any doubt.

2090
02:02:02,717 --> 02:02:04,487
I doubted myself 1,200 times.

2091
02:02:05,287 --> 02:02:06,417
Don't do that.

2092
02:02:07,857 --> 02:02:09,087
For me,

2093
02:02:10,017 --> 02:02:11,587
BADA's best moment...

2094
02:02:11,957 --> 02:02:13,156
(Curious)

2095
02:02:13,157 --> 02:02:15,257
When I was making the finger flick dance,

2096
02:02:16,097 --> 02:02:19,426
she looked like she was between a rock...

2097
02:02:19,427 --> 02:02:21,267
and a hard place.

2098
02:02:21,767 --> 02:02:23,997
(The day the legendary finger flick dance was born)

2099
02:02:24,937 --> 02:02:26,437
(Confused)

2100
02:02:26,707 --> 02:02:28,506
(How do I make it look cool?)

2101
02:02:28,507 --> 02:02:29,536
(Scratching)

2102
02:02:29,537 --> 02:02:31,857
(Even when they were presenting it in front of TAEYONG...)

2103
02:02:32,207 --> 02:02:33,576
(Her head bowed at the dance.)

2104
02:02:33,577 --> 02:02:34,777
I heard about it.

2105
02:02:34,847 --> 02:02:36,877
It wasn't BADA's cup of tea.

2106
02:02:37,117 --> 02:02:38,547
(She's caught.)

2107
02:02:38,887 --> 02:02:39,947
Back then,

2108
02:02:40,587 --> 02:02:44,156
I thought I should trust you wholeheartedly since we were a team.

2109
02:02:44,157 --> 02:02:45,756
But your face showed it all.

2110
02:02:45,757 --> 02:02:47,056
I'm looking forward to it.

2111
02:02:47,057 --> 02:02:49,296
- I'm waiting for that scene to air. - The finger flick dance.

2112
02:02:49,297 --> 02:02:51,327
- I agree. - I'm serious.

2113
02:02:51,497 --> 02:02:53,267
Sometimes, the song needs...

2114
02:02:53,797 --> 02:02:55,337
a character.

2115
02:02:55,467 --> 02:02:57,336
When you go home after practicing the Last Stage,

2116
02:02:57,337 --> 02:02:59,936
- you can't watch the show fully. - Yes.

2117
02:02:59,937 --> 02:03:01,783
As soon as I turned on the TV, it showed me "again."

2118
02:03:01,807 --> 02:03:03,136
(The one sentence that will go down in the show's history)

2119
02:03:03,137 --> 02:03:06,877
(Again.)

2120
02:03:07,547 --> 02:03:08,877
It was so funny.

2121
02:03:10,377 --> 02:03:12,087
(His "again" eyes are on.)

2122
02:03:12,287 --> 02:03:13,316
Again.

2123
02:03:13,317 --> 02:03:14,687
(Koo Young, again?)

2124
02:03:15,187 --> 02:03:16,617
(Please spare me.)

2125
02:03:16,857 --> 02:03:19,286
I really liked his facial expressions.

2126
02:03:19,287 --> 02:03:21,457
I can't forget the face he made...

2127
02:03:21,697 --> 02:03:23,827
for the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

2128
02:03:24,327 --> 02:03:26,296
(During the choreography match of 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

2129
02:03:26,297 --> 02:03:27,836
(BABYZOO was his loveliest self.)

2130
02:03:27,837 --> 02:03:29,167
(Getting immersed)

2131
02:03:29,667 --> 02:03:30,966
(Copying BABYZOO)

2132
02:03:30,967 --> 02:03:32,067
It's different.

2133
02:03:32,637 --> 02:03:34,537
(Here's the original.)

2134
02:03:35,207 --> 02:03:36,437
I'm embarrassed!

2135
02:03:37,647 --> 02:03:38,807
- Cute. - Thank you.

2136
02:03:39,677 --> 02:03:41,716
I like the way you talk.

2137
02:03:41,717 --> 02:03:44,347
"He must think he's innovative, right?"

2138
02:03:44,787 --> 02:03:45,916
(He must think...)

2139
02:03:45,917 --> 02:03:47,316
(he has...)

2140
02:03:47,317 --> 02:03:48,617
(a lot of ideas, right?)

2141
02:03:48,717 --> 02:03:50,956
You make perfect metaphors.

2142
02:03:50,957 --> 02:03:53,227
I was first shocked at the instant rice metaphor.

2143
02:03:53,487 --> 02:03:55,356
("Instant rice" metaphor)

2144
02:03:55,357 --> 02:03:57,126
(You arrive at the destination, drive three hours, )

2145
02:03:57,127 --> 02:03:59,066
(go through all the trouble to find it, )

2146
02:03:59,067 --> 02:04:00,936
(and bring back to Korea...)

2147
02:04:00,937 --> 02:04:02,137
(the instant rice.)

2148
02:04:02,437 --> 02:04:04,266
("Sweet potato or potato" metaphor)

2149
02:04:04,267 --> 02:04:06,836
(If you like something plain, potatoes for you.)

2150
02:04:06,837 --> 02:04:08,997
(If you like something sweet, sweet potatoes for you.)

2151
02:04:09,077 --> 02:04:10,077
(Like squid and peanuts, )

2152
02:04:10,078 --> 02:04:11,107
(like soju and beer.)

2153
02:04:11,347 --> 02:04:14,106
(We both bought a product. I read the whole user manual, )

2154
02:04:14,107 --> 02:04:15,447
(but they didn't.)

2155
02:04:15,647 --> 02:04:17,016
(Does it make sense to invite the singer Insooni...)

2156
02:04:17,017 --> 02:04:18,487
(and make her rap?)

2157
02:04:18,887 --> 02:04:20,547
They fit the situations perfectly.

2158
02:04:21,157 --> 02:04:24,587
I really like your directing too,

2159
02:04:24,887 --> 02:04:27,157
but that scene really made me question my eyes.

2160
02:04:27,227 --> 02:04:28,596
(Back Koo Young's new signature choreography)

2161
02:04:28,597 --> 02:04:30,197
- When you did this... - I agree.

2162
02:04:31,127 --> 02:04:32,997
You got on your knees...

2163
02:04:33,327 --> 02:04:35,836
and did this. That scene is stuck in my memory like a photo.

2164
02:04:35,837 --> 02:04:37,537
(His knee dance shocked everyone.)

2165
02:04:37,737 --> 02:04:39,267
I still remember.

2166
02:04:39,507 --> 02:04:41,607
I was looking at the floor like this.

2167
02:04:41,777 --> 02:04:43,677
Suddenly, someone went down.

2168
02:04:44,647 --> 02:04:46,907
I thought, "Why is he doing this?"

2169
02:04:47,347 --> 02:04:49,146
It was so shocking...

2170
02:04:49,147 --> 02:04:50,987
that I remember it like a photo.

2171
02:04:51,147 --> 02:04:53,047
I can't forget that moment.

2172
02:04:53,887 --> 02:04:57,187
But it became a really good trigger for me.

2173
02:04:57,787 --> 02:04:59,456
I learned so much...

2174
02:04:59,457 --> 02:05:02,096
while being on this show.

2175
02:05:02,097 --> 02:05:03,996
From song production...

2176
02:05:03,997 --> 02:05:06,327
to stage production, lighting,

2177
02:05:06,667 --> 02:05:08,196
special effects,

2178
02:05:08,197 --> 02:05:11,337
when to use a VJ source...

2179
02:05:11,537 --> 02:05:14,136
Every moment was shocking.

2180
02:05:14,137 --> 02:05:15,307
"Even this?"

2181
02:05:15,377 --> 02:05:17,006
"They went this far?"

2182
02:05:17,007 --> 02:05:18,477
I learned a lot.

2183
02:05:18,777 --> 02:05:22,246
As I continue to live my life as a director,

2184
02:05:22,247 --> 02:05:24,046
it'll help me a lot.

2185
02:05:24,047 --> 02:05:25,516
I learned so much from the other directors...

2186
02:05:25,517 --> 02:05:27,417
while working on this show.

2187
02:05:27,687 --> 02:05:29,157
Whenever I did my job,

2188
02:05:29,657 --> 02:05:32,687
I thought I was playing the supporting role.

2189
02:05:33,127 --> 02:05:35,157
I needed to take care of so many things.

2190
02:05:35,727 --> 02:05:38,497
But seeing how passionate everyone was,

2191
02:05:40,227 --> 02:05:42,397
it made me realize how I should work.

2192
02:05:42,597 --> 02:05:45,606
Watching the other directors...

2193
02:05:45,607 --> 02:05:47,777
became the stepping stone to my own improvement.

2194
02:05:48,037 --> 02:05:49,937
Tae Woo,

2195
02:05:50,207 --> 02:05:53,547
when it came to lighting and stage production,

2196
02:05:53,877 --> 02:05:57,146
you showed me so many things I couldn't even think of.

2197
02:05:57,147 --> 02:05:58,686
As I saw that,

2198
02:05:58,687 --> 02:06:00,747
I thought I should study hard...

2199
02:06:00,887 --> 02:06:03,257
and become like you guys.

2200
02:06:03,557 --> 02:06:06,427
Personally, from this show,

2201
02:06:06,957 --> 02:06:09,697
I learned to give it my all.

2202
02:06:10,097 --> 02:06:11,297
Me too.

2203
02:06:11,367 --> 02:06:14,866
Actually, when you work outside of the show,

2204
02:06:14,867 --> 02:06:16,567
it's hard to get a job...

2205
02:06:16,967 --> 02:06:20,107
which allows you to give it your all.

2206
02:06:20,237 --> 02:06:22,206
I make something good and deliver it,

2207
02:06:22,207 --> 02:06:23,607
and that's my job done.

2208
02:06:23,807 --> 02:06:26,706
That's how I've been treating my job so far.

2209
02:06:26,707 --> 02:06:28,447
But on this show,

2210
02:06:28,717 --> 02:06:32,017
working with the dancers...

2211
02:06:32,547 --> 02:06:35,287
and directing the artist...

2212
02:06:35,817 --> 02:06:38,087
made me realize how fun directing was.

2213
02:06:38,427 --> 02:06:41,627
I felt happy while directing.

2214
02:06:42,627 --> 02:06:44,467
(I can do it.)

2215
02:06:45,327 --> 02:06:47,967
I worked on each production with utmost sincerity.

2216
02:06:48,197 --> 02:06:51,807
And I got to grow. It was fun.

2217
02:06:52,567 --> 02:06:54,836
Thinking and researching...

2218
02:06:54,837 --> 02:06:56,407
It was time well spent.

2219
02:06:57,407 --> 02:06:59,106
Koo Young,

2220
02:06:59,107 --> 02:07:01,576
You memorized all the dancers' names you performed with.

2221
02:07:01,577 --> 02:07:03,316
I think you memorize their names all the time.

2222
02:07:03,317 --> 02:07:04,717
- Kids dancers too. - All the time.

2223
02:07:04,917 --> 02:07:05,987
To be honest,

2224
02:07:06,787 --> 02:07:08,557
I feel thankful.

2225
02:07:09,457 --> 02:07:11,856
They call me by my name.

2226
02:07:11,857 --> 02:07:14,426
When we call each other by our names to communicate,

2227
02:07:14,427 --> 02:07:18,066
we feel good, I guess.

2228
02:07:18,067 --> 02:07:20,626
- From our perspective, that's so... - Right.

2229
02:07:20,627 --> 02:07:21,836
That night, I would realize...

2230
02:07:21,837 --> 02:07:23,396
that Koo Young remembers my name...

2231
02:07:23,397 --> 02:07:24,906
- and that one thing... - Exactly.

2232
02:07:24,907 --> 02:07:26,207
Can cheer me up to go on.

2233
02:07:26,507 --> 02:07:29,476
In a way, the big title of Baek Koo Young,

2234
02:07:29,477 --> 02:07:33,146
and BADA, BABYZOO, and Kasper are the big titles to show.

2235
02:07:33,147 --> 02:07:36,317
But all the other dancers do their best for our performances.

2236
02:07:37,177 --> 02:07:39,817
I feel more thankful to them than usual.

2237
02:07:40,187 --> 02:07:42,886
From the 400 Mission to now,

2238
02:07:42,887 --> 02:07:45,887
there are dancers who helped us,

2239
02:07:46,487 --> 02:07:48,797
and I appreciate that.

2240
02:07:48,897 --> 02:07:51,497
Without them, we can't make the performance happen.

2241
02:07:52,067 --> 02:07:55,996
In fact, I want to have an occasion that all of us gather together.

2242
02:07:55,997 --> 02:07:57,736
- That will be lovely. - Yes.

2243
02:07:57,737 --> 02:08:01,176
I'd like to have an opportunity to repay the gratitude.

2244
02:08:01,177 --> 02:08:02,177
It will be fun.

2245
02:08:02,178 --> 02:08:04,007
It will be loud, though.

2246
02:08:05,007 --> 02:08:06,007
I think it will be fun.

2247
02:08:06,008 --> 02:08:07,288
Are you going to treat everyone?

2248
02:08:07,447 --> 02:08:08,476
It will be on me.

2249
02:08:08,477 --> 02:08:10,317
(Directors send their respect to all dancers.)

2250
02:08:11,117 --> 02:08:13,387
- To your positions! - Everyone to your positions!

2251
02:08:13,987 --> 02:08:15,756
(Director's Square looks unfamiliar today.)

2252
02:08:15,757 --> 02:08:17,477
I wish they would eat as much as they like.

2253
02:08:17,557 --> 02:08:19,856
Today, it's "Respect to All Dancers."

2254
02:08:19,857 --> 02:08:21,596
We will bring our dancers...

2255
02:08:21,597 --> 02:08:23,896
and express our gratitude.

2256
02:08:23,897 --> 02:08:25,826
We will enjoy dinner together.

2257
02:08:25,827 --> 02:08:28,366
In Directors' Square today,

2258
02:08:28,367 --> 02:08:30,696
I'm hearing music that hasn't been played so far.

2259
02:08:30,697 --> 02:08:32,466
- Weeoo, weeoo. - Weeoo, weeoo.

2260
02:08:32,467 --> 02:08:33,936
I've only heard these. I think I'll hear it in my dream.

2261
02:08:33,937 --> 02:08:35,176
But now I'm hearing pleasant music.

2262
02:08:35,177 --> 02:08:37,477
This place feels different to me now.

2263
02:08:37,877 --> 02:08:39,776
You should have played this kind of music more often.

2264
02:08:39,777 --> 02:08:41,246
I know. You're right.

2265
02:08:41,247 --> 02:08:42,876
I hope they enjoy this.

2266
02:08:42,877 --> 02:08:45,316
They should eat this parsley too.

2267
02:08:45,317 --> 02:08:47,616
Parsley is a vegetable. It's good for your health.

2268
02:08:47,617 --> 02:08:50,757
A nicely plated food will whet your appetite.

2269
02:08:50,817 --> 02:08:53,286
I will plate the dessert first.

2270
02:08:53,287 --> 02:08:55,226
Preparing food is important,

2271
02:08:55,227 --> 02:08:56,956
but decoration is also important.

2272
02:08:56,957 --> 02:08:59,466
They're the ones who light up the stage,

2273
02:08:59,467 --> 02:09:01,397
so I will light up candles here.

2274
02:09:01,497 --> 02:09:03,266
If you light up the stage, it's lighting?

2275
02:09:03,267 --> 02:09:04,466
The master of lighting?

2276
02:09:04,467 --> 02:09:06,336
Do I need to place blueberries upside down?

2277
02:09:06,337 --> 02:09:08,706
You can see a person's aesthetic taste here.

2278
02:09:08,707 --> 02:09:10,877
(4 finalists are busy preparing for the dinner.)

2279
02:09:11,077 --> 02:09:12,206
Okay. We're done now.

2280
02:09:12,207 --> 02:09:13,507
I think they will love it.

2281
02:09:13,777 --> 02:09:15,476
Now I realize we're coming to an end.

2282
02:09:15,477 --> 02:09:16,816
- The music feels... - Happy.

2283
02:09:16,817 --> 02:09:18,516
And all of a sudden...

2284
02:09:18,517 --> 02:09:19,986
(They still have a siren trauma.)

2285
02:09:19,987 --> 02:09:21,017
I hope not.

2286
02:09:21,787 --> 02:09:22,787
What's this?

2287
02:09:22,788 --> 02:09:24,157
(His body is moving by instinct.)

2288
02:09:25,187 --> 02:09:27,026
Here they are.

2289
02:09:27,027 --> 02:09:28,027
(Exclaiming)

2290
02:09:28,557 --> 02:09:30,633
(The first guests arrived are dancers invited by BADA.)

2291
02:09:30,657 --> 02:09:33,797
(I cast them first for the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.)

2292
02:09:34,327 --> 02:09:35,336
(Jinwoo.)

2293
02:09:35,337 --> 02:09:36,337
(You're mine.)

2294
02:09:36,437 --> 02:09:39,157
(Jinwoo and Hyun Se joined her in the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.)

2295
02:09:39,367 --> 02:09:40,907
Koo Young!

2296
02:09:41,277 --> 02:09:43,437
(Next, dancers invited by Baek Koo Young enter.)

2297
02:09:43,607 --> 02:09:44,977
Here you are.

2298
02:09:45,107 --> 02:09:47,177
Hi. Hello.

2299
02:09:47,347 --> 02:09:48,946
- It's him. - For...

2300
02:09:48,947 --> 02:09:50,576
the last performance,

2301
02:09:50,577 --> 02:09:53,587
he became an offering on the altar.

2302
02:09:54,657 --> 02:09:57,316
This guy played the role that made the biggest sacrifice.

2303
02:09:57,317 --> 02:09:58,457
He's Hyun Sung.

2304
02:09:59,987 --> 02:10:02,827
(Dancers invited by BABYZOO enter.)

2305
02:10:02,927 --> 02:10:06,497
My first mission was 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

2306
02:10:06,567 --> 02:10:08,936
I could make it thanks to these four dancers.

2307
02:10:08,937 --> 02:10:10,837
That's why I invited them here.

2308
02:10:11,167 --> 02:10:12,937
(Welcome.)

2309
02:10:13,267 --> 02:10:14,977
(She found something.)

2310
02:10:15,137 --> 02:10:16,907
(All eyes on)

2311
02:10:17,377 --> 02:10:19,247
This is insane.

2312
02:10:19,507 --> 02:10:21,617
Hello.

2313
02:10:22,917 --> 02:10:26,086
Who keeps doing those unexpected things?

2314
02:10:26,087 --> 02:10:27,587
You're doing it to embarrass him.

2315
02:10:30,157 --> 02:10:32,227
- Hello. - Come on.

2316
02:10:32,527 --> 02:10:34,796
This guy is actually the ultimate backstabber.

2317
02:10:34,797 --> 02:10:36,527
- He was in 1MILLION... - The turncoat.

2318
02:10:36,757 --> 02:10:38,596
Calm down.

2319
02:10:38,597 --> 02:10:40,126
He was in 1MILLION,

2320
02:10:40,127 --> 02:10:41,796
but now he's become my sworn brother.

2321
02:10:41,797 --> 02:10:43,097
Here's Nino.

2322
02:10:43,337 --> 02:10:45,336
(Kasper's first casting dancer, Nino)

2323
02:10:45,337 --> 02:10:46,706
(Nino joined him on many missions like Title Sequence Film Mission...)

2324
02:10:46,707 --> 02:10:48,006
(and K-Pop Solo Artist Directing Mission.)

2325
02:10:48,007 --> 02:10:50,476
One is missing today, but here's Penrose.

2326
02:10:50,477 --> 02:10:51,946
(Kasper's must-have item for the stage, Penrose. Yun Min Soo)

2327
02:10:51,947 --> 02:10:53,877
(Lee Kyung Woo)

2328
02:10:54,177 --> 02:10:55,476
Thank you for coming!

2329
02:10:55,477 --> 02:10:56,917
Thank you!

2330
02:10:57,017 --> 02:10:58,246
Please enjoy...

2331
02:10:58,247 --> 02:11:00,687
the small but precious feast we prepared.

2332
02:11:01,417 --> 02:11:03,756
(Great!)

2333
02:11:03,757 --> 02:11:04,886
Yes!

2334
02:11:04,887 --> 02:11:06,626
Thank you for the food.

2335
02:11:06,627 --> 02:11:08,296
Eat your fill, and have some more.

2336
02:11:08,297 --> 02:11:09,527
Thank you for the food.

2337
02:11:09,557 --> 02:11:10,657
(Having a big bite)

2338
02:11:11,467 --> 02:11:12,627
Is it good?

2339
02:11:13,467 --> 02:11:15,436
The Kids Mission was really funny.

2340
02:11:15,437 --> 02:11:17,997
- "Again." - I found that so funny.

2341
02:11:18,267 --> 02:11:19,267
"Again."

2342
02:11:19,537 --> 02:11:20,537
(What's going on?)

2343
02:11:20,538 --> 02:11:22,807
("RUDE!" is suddenly played.)

2344
02:11:23,237 --> 02:11:24,237
What's going on?

2345
02:11:24,238 --> 02:11:25,347
(What's happening?)

2346
02:11:27,507 --> 02:11:28,516
(Startled)

2347
02:11:28,517 --> 02:11:29,817
(Seung Min suddenly appears.)

2348
02:11:30,247 --> 02:11:32,016
He will be really surprised if I show up all of a sudden.

2349
02:11:32,017 --> 02:11:33,046
I'm so nervous.

2350
02:11:33,047 --> 02:11:34,347
Oh, my goodness.

2351
02:11:35,157 --> 02:11:36,157
What?

2352
02:11:36,158 --> 02:11:38,227
(Seung Min in Team BABYZOO came in secret.)

2353
02:11:38,427 --> 02:11:39,786
Why me, of all the dancers?

2354
02:11:39,787 --> 02:11:42,127
Why am I the first one?

2355
02:11:42,157 --> 02:11:43,897
(On edge)

2356
02:11:44,397 --> 02:11:45,467
(Dashing out)

2357
02:11:46,667 --> 02:11:48,997
You know what he said to me?

2358
02:11:49,437 --> 02:11:51,437
(Here I am.)

2359
02:11:52,107 --> 02:11:53,107
What's going on?

2360
02:11:53,108 --> 02:11:55,077
You missed me, right?

2361
02:11:55,507 --> 02:11:56,706
What's happening?

2362
02:11:56,707 --> 02:11:57,737
(Shocked)

2363
02:11:59,207 --> 02:12:00,806
(Suddenly breaking into a dance)

2364
02:12:00,807 --> 02:12:03,017
(The surprise guest shocks the dancers.)

2365
02:12:03,617 --> 02:12:04,947
What's going on?

2366
02:12:06,647 --> 02:12:09,056
(The surprise appearance is a huge success.)

2367
02:12:09,057 --> 02:12:10,386
How are you?

2368
02:12:10,387 --> 02:12:12,287
I'm a surprise gift!

2369
02:12:12,887 --> 02:12:13,956
Oh, my!

2370
02:12:13,957 --> 02:12:15,156
(BABYZOO's surprise guest, Dancer Seung Min)

2371
02:12:15,157 --> 02:12:16,726
You said you couldn't come.

2372
02:12:16,727 --> 02:12:18,267
I was lying, of course.

2373
02:12:18,427 --> 02:12:21,126
Seung Min stepped up in the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

2374
02:12:21,127 --> 02:12:22,836
He gave a surprise performance,

2375
02:12:22,837 --> 02:12:25,267
and it was so reassuring and moving.

2376
02:12:26,107 --> 02:12:27,166
I should come, of course.

2377
02:12:27,167 --> 02:12:28,707
How can I miss this?

2378
02:12:30,407 --> 02:12:31,407
(Really amazed)

2379
02:12:31,507 --> 02:12:32,946
"How can I miss this?"

2380
02:12:32,947 --> 02:12:34,576
Did you see him outside?

2381
02:12:34,577 --> 02:12:36,846
- No, I haven't seen him at all. - I told no one.

2382
02:12:36,847 --> 02:12:38,847
- Where have you been hiding? - Over there.

2383
02:12:39,017 --> 02:12:40,416
(Music plays again.)

2384
02:12:40,417 --> 02:12:41,857
(Is there another one?)

2385
02:12:42,187 --> 02:12:43,456
